# =============================================================================
# storage-service — peticiones de prueba (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP)
# =============================================================================
# Requiere la extension "REST Client" (humao.rest-client) en VS Code.
# Ajusta @apiKey al valor de API_KEY de tu .env.
# Cada bloque separado por ### es una peticion ejecutable ("Send Request").
#
# Las subidas multipart usan la sintaxis "< ./ruta" para adjuntar un archivo
# del disco: crea uno de prueba o cambia la ruta por uno que exista.
# =============================================================================

@host = http://localhost:3010
# Emitir con: npm run register:apikey -- --name "pruebas" (la key se muestra
# una sola vez; requiere un bucket/app registrados con register-bucket).
@apiKey = sk_reemplazar_por_una_key_emitida
# Access token de auth_ws (via Bearer, requiere AUTH_WS_BASE_URL configurada):
# obtenerlo con el flujo de login de auth_ws (POST /auth/login -> /auth/sessions).
@accessToken = pegar_un_access_token_de_auth_ws


### Health — no requiere api key
GET {{host}}/health


### Buckets disponibles y sus limites
GET {{host}}/v1/buckets
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


### Subir en JSON (base64) — minimo: filename + contenido
# @name uploadJson
POST {{host}}/v1/files
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "filename": "nota.txt",
  "content_base64": "SG9sYSBkZXNkZSBzdG9yYWdlLXNlcnZpY2UK"
}


### Subir en JSON completo (ruta, bucket, tipo y metadata)
POST {{host}}/v1/files
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "filename": "factura-4711.pdf",
  "path": "2026/08/factura-4711.pdf",
  "bucket_code": "invoices",
  "content_type": "application/pdf",
  "content_base64": "JVBERi0xLjQKJSVFT0YK",
  "metadata": { "order_id": "4711", "tipo": "factura" }
}


### Subir multipart (streaming) — la via para archivos grandes
# @name uploadMultipart
POST {{host}}/v1/files
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----storage

------storage
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="path"

docs/2026/informe.txt
------storage
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="metadata"

{"origen":"requests.http"}
------storage
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="informe.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./package.json
------storage--


### Subir el MISMO contenido a otra ruta -> deduplicated: true
POST {{host}}/v1/files
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "filename": "nota-copia.txt",
  "path": "docs/nota-copia.txt",
  "content_base64": "SG9sYSBkZXNkZSBzdG9yYWdlLXNlcnZpY2UK"
}


### Metadata por id (usa el id devuelto por la subida JSON)
GET {{host}}/v1/files/{{uploadJson.response.body.id}}
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


### Metadata por ruta — sin haber guardado el id
GET {{host}}/v1/files?path=nota.txt
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


### Listado por prefijo, paginado
GET {{host}}/v1/files?prefix=docs/&limit=20
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


### Descargar con api key
GET {{host}}/v1/files/{{uploadJson.response.body.id}}/content
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


### Descargar forzando "guardar como"
GET {{host}}/v1/files/{{uploadJson.response.body.id}}/content?download=1
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


### Descargar un tramo -> 206 + Content-Range
GET {{host}}/v1/files/{{uploadJson.response.body.id}}/content
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Range: bytes=0-9


### Los ultimos bytes (sufijo) -> 206
GET {{host}}/v1/files/{{uploadJson.response.body.id}}/content
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Range: bytes=-5


### Tramo fuera del archivo -> 416 + Content-Range: bytes *\/tamaño
GET {{host}}/v1/files/{{uploadJson.response.body.id}}/content
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Range: bytes=99999999-


### Emitir un enlace temporal firmado (5 min)
# @name link
POST {{host}}/v1/files/{{uploadJson.response.body.id}}/link
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "expires_in_sec": 300 }


### Descargar por el enlace firmado — SIN api key
GET {{link.response.body.url}}


### Borrado logico -> 204
DELETE {{host}}/v1/files/{{uploadJson.response.body.id}}
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


# =============================================================================
# Via access token (usuario final) — requiere AUTH_WS_BASE_URL y que la sesion
# tenga los permisos storage.files.* en el catalogo de su app
# =============================================================================

### Listar archivos con el Bearer del usuario (permiso storage.files.read)
GET {{host}}/v1/files?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### Subir con el Bearer del usuario (permiso storage.files.write)
POST {{host}}/v1/files
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "filename": "nota-usuario.txt",
  "path": "usuarios/nota.txt",
  "content_base64": "SG9sYSBjb24gYWNjZXNzIHRva2VuCg=="
}


### Emitir enlace firmado con el Bearer (permiso storage.files.share)
POST {{host}}/v1/files/{{uploadJson.response.body.id}}/link
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{ "expires_in_sec": 300 }


# =============================================================================
# Casos de error esperados
# =============================================================================

### Sin api key -> 401
GET {{host}}/v1/files?path=nota.txt


### Api key invalida -> 401
GET {{host}}/v1/buckets
X-Api-Key: key-invalida


### Body invalido: sin contenido -> 400
POST {{host}}/v1/files
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "filename": "vacio.txt" }


### Bucket inexistente por code -> 422
POST {{host}}/v1/files
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "filename": "x.txt",
  "bucket_code": "no-existe-este-bucket",
  "content_base64": "eAo="
}


### MIME fuera de la lista blanca del bucket -> 415
POST {{host}}/v1/files
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "filename": "imagen.png",
  "content_type": "image/png",
  "content_base64": "iVBORw0KGgo="
}


### Id inexistente -> 404
GET {{host}}/v1/files/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}


### Enlace con firma alterada -> 403
GET {{host}}/v1/public/files/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000/content?expires=9999999999&sig=firma-invalida
